# the American and Saigon sides, as the history dates them
A('1961-0619-staley', '1961-06-19', 'vietnam', 'Kennedy sends a "special economic mission" under Eugene Staley of the Stanford Research Institute to South Vietnam, June 19, to help Diệm draw up the pacification program. After nearly a month of talks with Saigon officials and with Diệm, the mission reports to Kennedy at the end of July.', 'III, 16', also=['vietnam-saigon'], tags=US + ['ok:fields-place'], extra='Names: Eugene Staley.', check='the history dates the mission\'s start June 19; the Staley report is [[cal.1961-07-14.vietnam]].')
A('1961-0917-thompson', '1961-09-17', 'vietnam', 'A British advisory mission on administration and policy, led by Robert Thompson, the counterguerrilla expert of Malaya, arrives Sept. 17 at Diệm\'s invitation as adviser on pacification.', 'III, 168', also=['vietnam-saigon'], tags=US + ['name:thompson-robert'], extra='Names: Robert Thompson.', check='the history gives "Sept. 17" without the arrival; the American record not read.')
A('1961-04-zones', '1961-04', 'vietnam-saigon', 'Saigon changes its military regions into tactical zones, each under a main-force corps with its local forces and supporting arms; below the zone, tactical areas, sectors (provinces) and subsectors (districts). Saigon–Gia Định a "capital special zone". American advisers and supporting units, the helicopter and air transport units above all, are put down to the zones.', 'III, 25', when='Apr.', also=['vietnam'], tags=RV + ['polity:us', 'ok:fields-place'], check='the day.')
A('1963-early-ivcorps', '1963', 'vietnam-saigon', 'In early 1963 the provinces of the Mekong delta are separated from the 3d tactical zone to make a 4th.', 'III, 25 n.1', when='1963, early', at='before 1963-01', also=['vietnam'], tags=RV + ['ok:fields-place'], check='the day.')
A('1962-04-hamlets', '1962-04', 'vietnam', 'From April Saigon and the Americans carry out over the whole South the program of gathering the people into "strategic hamlets", after trials in some places in Tây Ninh, Bình Dương, Biên Hòa and Quảng Ngãi. The aim: 10 million peasants in 16,000 of 17,000 hamlets planned, and a pacification apparatus, with American advisers alongside, from the center to the provinces.', 'III, 26', when='Apr.', also=['vietnam-saigon'], tags=RV + ['polity:us', 'ok:fields-place'], check='the day; compare [[cal.1962-03-22.vietnam]], Operation Sunrise.')
K('cal.1963-08-24.vietnam-3', 'Check: the history adds that the police broke up the Aug. 25 rally, the student Quách Thị Trang was killed and nearly 200 young men and women taken to the Quang Trung training center (III, 313).')
A('1964-0516-reorg', '1964-05-16', 'vietnam-saigon', 'Nguyễn Khánh reorganizes his government, May 16.', 'III, 320 n.1', names=['Nguyễn Khánh'], also=['vietnam'], tags=RV + ['ok:fields-place'], check='the history gives the day in a list of coups and reorganizations; the American record not read.')
A('1965-0212-sau', '1965-02-12', 'vietnam-saigon', 'Taylor "arranges" a government with Phan Khắc Sửu as chief of state and Phan Huy Quát as premier, Feb. 12, by the history\'s list.', 'III, 320 n.1', names=['Phan Khắc Sửu', 'Phan Huy Quát'], also=['vietnam'], tags=RV + ['polity:us', 'ok:fields-place'], check='the history\'s date; the Quát government took office later in February; the American record not read.')
A('1965-0306-coup', '1965-03-06', 'vietnam-saigon', 'A coup against Phan Huy Quát\'s government fails, Mar. 6, the first of three, by the history\'s list.', 'III, 320 n.1', also=['vietnam'], tags=RV + ['ok:fields-place'], check='the history gives the date in a list; the American record not read.')
A('1965-0420-coup', '1965-04-20', 'vietnam-saigon', 'A coup against Phan Huy Quát\'s government fails, Apr. 20, the second of three, by the history\'s list.', 'III, 320 n.1', also=['vietnam'], tags=RV + ['ok:fields-place'], check='the history gives the date in a list; the American record not read.')
# the DRV's day of Aug. 5, 1964
A('1964-0805-cuahoi', '1964-08-05', VH, 'Nghệ An. 12:30 p.m., Aug. 5, eight American aircraft bomb Cửa Hội. The antiaircraft of the navy\'s ships and of the shore shoot down one, 2 km west of Hòn Mắt island.', 'III, 368', time='12:30', tz='Asia/Bangkok', place='cua-hoi', also=AW + ['vietnam'], check='the clock is Hanoi\'s; compare [[cal.1964-08-05.vietnam]].')
A('1964-0805-gianh1', '1964-08-05', VH, 'Quảng Bình. Aug. 5 a flight of eight American aircraft, coming from the west behind the mountains, bombs the Gianh river port. The antiaircraft posts and navy ships with the militia of Cảnh Dương commune shoot down one into the sea and hit another.', 'III, 368', place='gianh-river', also=AW + ['vietnam'], tags=['ok:fields-time'], check='the hour; the history places the flight after the Cửa Hội raid of 12:30.')
A('1964-0805-honggai', '1964-08-05', VH, 'Quảng Ninh. Aug. 5 a flight of eight American aircraft dives on Hòn Gai and Bãi Cháy. An A4 is hit and falls into the sea at Hà Tu; its pilot, Lt. Everett Alvarez, parachutes. Sgt. Nguyễn Kim Bảo of the Northeast Military Region, with two border guards on a boat for Cô Tô island, and local militia including Bác Lộc, take him alive.', 'III, 368', place='hon-gai', names=['Nguyễn Kim Bảo'], also=AW + ['vietnam'], extra='', tags=['ok:fields-time'], check='the hour; Alvarez\'s name as the history prints it, "I. Anvơrét"; compare [[cal.1964-08-05.vietnam]].')
A('1964-0805-baichay', '1964-08-05', VH, 'Quảng Ninh. 2:45 p.m., Aug. 5, American aircraft again hit Bãi Cháy and Lạch Trường. Three are shot down, one hit.', 'III, 368', time='14:45', tz='Asia/Bangkok', place='bai-chay', also=AW + ['vietnam'], check='the clock is Hanoi\'s.')
A('1964-0805-gianh2', '1964-08-05', VH, 'Quảng Bình. 4:20 p.m., Aug. 5, American aircraft bomb the Gianh river port a second time. The antiaircraft and the militia shoot down two: one 25 km out at sea, one at Cự Nẫm, Bố Trạch.', 'III, 368', time='16:20', tz='Asia/Bangkok', place='gianh-river', also=AW + ['vietnam'], check='the clock is Hanoi\'s.')
A('1964-0805-cuahoi2', '1964-08-05', VH, 'Nghệ An. The afternoon of Aug. 5 eight American aircraft again dive on Cửa Hội; the fire drives them off.', 'III, 368', place='cua-hoi', band_='afternoon', tz='Asia/Bangkok', also=AW + ['vietnam'])
